# Vanilla: Expanded TODO List:
    ## Issues:
        ☐ Make game start paused by default.
        ☐ BUG: Quern auto stash not working for items which the base game prefers not to merge (e.g. perishable foods which have a large difference in freshness). FIX: the quern should force merge items when auto stashing.
        ☐ Design a better separation of alloy calculator inventory ownership/liveness validation, transfer permissions, and storage-versus-machine access policy. Reconsider the storage-class whitelist without weakening ownership or withdrawal checks, and define coverage for vanilla and modded containers.
        ☐ Prevent "Equip light source" hotkey from triggering when the player is holding a hammer and has tongs equipped in offhand.
        ☑ Fix fractional Cairo text placement in radial-progress labels: round final framebuffer X/Y immediately before drawing in RadialProgressBarRenderer. Preserve natural texture dimensions; cover odd texture/screen dimensions, fractional ring positions/sizes, and auto-stashing/auto-looting labels. Draw-boundary and hold-progress tests pass; live-game verification remains in the shared verification task.
        ☐ Fix conditional fractional placement of text-bearing tool-mode textures: establish how borrowed SkillItem textures containing Cairo text are identified, then snap their final placement in ToolModeSkillIcon, including the non-premultiplied branch. Preserve ordinary icon behavior and render text at natural size rather than resizing its cached texture.
        ☐ Fix conditional text scaling/fractional placement in tool-mode RenderHandler callbacks: establish a text-aware rendering contract so cached Cairo text is not affected by the icon translate/scale transform. Cover fractional centers and non-unit icon scales while preserving artwork scaling and restoring render state.
        ☐ Harden native text-control placement independently of engine truncation (not a confirmed placement bug in Vintage Story 1.22.7): explicitly snap final text placement for HUD style dropdown values, size inputs, action buttons, and corresponding alloy-calculator controls. Do not round only parent bounds; account for centering and input scroll offsets, preserve input/hit-testing behavior, and avoid global changes to unrelated game UI.
        ☐ Verify the Cairo text-placement fixes with draw-boundary tests and live-game checks at multiple GUI scales: final texture origins must be integer framebuffer pixels and text textures must retain natural dimensions. Include tool-mode callback transforms and confirm existing HUD readings, radial-menu labels, tooltips, expanded lists, group captions, and dialog text remain correct.

    ## New Features:
        ☐ Add a "Todo List" feature which allows players to create their own ingame tasks and reminders.
        ☐ Targeted items such as tools on toolracks have a subtle highlight to indicate that they are targeted.

    ## Death Penalties:
        ☐ New death penalty option: lose *bag* items on death (items in inventory are lost, items on hotbar and equipped armor and weapons are kept).
        ☐ New death penalty option: lose *unequipped* items on death (items in inventory and hotbar are lost, equipped armor and weapons are kept).
        ☐ New death penalty option: lose *all* items on death (items in inventory, hotbar, equipped armor & weapons are lost).
        ☐ Tool degradation on death: all tools in inventory and hotbar lose <configurable percent> durability on death.

    ## Effects:
        ☐ Blocks with light level 1 have subtle haze/smoke particles (to indicate the edge of lit areas) (reuse the existing temporal storm ground particle effect).

# Vanilla: Rebalanced Ideas:
    Note: this is a different mod from Vanilla: Expanded, I'm just keeping the ideas list here for now.
    ## Recipes:
        ☐ Candles from animal fat (render fat into tallow -> tallow replaces wax in candle recipe).

    ## Monster Rebalancing:
        ☐ Monsters cant spawn under roofs.
        ☐ Increase gear drop rates from monsters (and trading costs for gears) by 500%. this will make fighting monsters feel more rewarding.
        ☐ Add other items to monster drops (bones, scrapmetal, metal parts (uncommon), gems (rare), etc) to make them more rewarding to fight.
